  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-MYS827</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity to improve implementation  of labour migration governance and enhancement of support services for migrant workers in line with the ILO Multilateral Framework and standards and ASEAN instruments.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO is actively supporting Malaysia in improving its labour migration governance through various Development Cooperation projects. This support includes strengthening policies and mechanisms for protecting migrant worker wages, extending social security coverage, and promoting fair recruitment practices. The ILO&apos;s efforts also focus on combating forced labor and trafficking, and ensuring access to decent work for migrant workers. 

Wage Protection:
The ILO is helping Malaysia strengthen its policies and mechanisms related to wage protection for migrant workers, particularly in the plantation, manufacturing, and electronics sectors. 

Social Security:
The ILO is working with Malaysia to extend social security coverage to foreign workers, with a focus on reaching hard-to-reach groups like domestic workers and fishers. 

Fair Recruitment:
The ILO supports Malaysia&apos;s efforts to move towards fair migration governance, addressing issues of forced labor and trade sanctions related to labor migration. 

Combating Forced Labour:
The ILO is assisting Malaysia in implementing its National Action Plan on Forced Labour and addressing issues of trafficking and forced labor in supply chains. It also works with the Sabah State government and stakeholders in child labour and skills development for young people mainly children of migrant workers.</narrative>
  </description>
